        <a class="commenterIcon js-tooltipTrigger tooltipTrigger" data-resource-id="693516" data-resource-type="User" data-extra="Group.4170" title="Larry (lomifeh) | 88 comments" href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/693516-larry"><img alt="Larry (lomifeh) | 88 comments" src="https://images.gr-assets.com/users/1197942471p1/693516.jpg" /></a>
      I've got to agree here, I am on my third re-read of the book and I am seeing things I missed before. I first read it when I was around 18 and then again around 30. Now I am 37 and see things I missed or things seem to make more sense. The book has, for me, aged very well as well. I notice a lot of my base conceptions about the characters have remained the same, I just seem to see some of their motivation better.
    <br/><br/>
  </div>
